X:1
T:Valse Op. 69 No. 2
C:Frédéric Chopin
O:Waltz in B minor, Op. 69 No. 2 (posthumous)
N:The opening period only (8 bars). Transposed down a major sixth from B minor to
N:D minor, so the lowest note is C#4 and the highest F5. Notes from two Humdrum
N:first-edition encodings (ifdo.ca, kern2abc) that agree, and the flutetunes.com
N:MIDI. The last bar stops after four eighths: the pickup F#5 of the next pass
N:takes the place of the original's last two eighths (F#5 C#5), so the tune
N:comes round evenly. Chords from the left hand of the flutetunes.com arrangement.
M:3/4
Q:1/4=132
L:1/8
K:Dm
